1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,760
After everything I just said, I have a question for you.

2
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:16,480
Do you feel like you're truly living, or do you spend too much time inside your head

3
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:19,460
thinking about what happened in the past and what might happen next?

4
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:21,740
If it's the second one, don't worry.

5
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:24,120
There's a character who can teach us how to stop doing that.

6
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:25,720
And that's Jake the Dog.

7
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,060
And the interesting thing is, he's practically a god.

8
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,760
Yet despite that, Jake chose to live like an ordinary mortal,

9
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:33,420
eating sandwiches and going on adventures.

10
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:35,620
So why did he choose to live that way?

11
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:38,020
The answer lies in his philosophy of life.

12
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:40,280
And once you understand the five virtues behind that philosophy,

13
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:43,680
you'll start questioning everything about the way you're living.

14
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,020
But to understand that,

15
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:47,460
we first need to understand his past.

16
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:50,160
Because Jake starts the series with a secret.

17
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:52,960
Jake wasn't always the happy-go-lucky dog we know.

18
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,120
In the episode "The Last Job,"

19
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:56,660
we learn that Jake used to be a criminal.

20
00:00:56,660 --> 00:01:00,320
He didn't just commit theft; he was also involved in organized crime.

21
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:02,680
And in fact, he was really good at it.

22
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:05,780
He was the only thief capable of pulling it off.

23
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:09,520
But one day, along his life of crime, Jake made a decision.

24
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:12,220
He walked away from that life and never looked back.

25
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:14,580
That decision shaped Jake's philosophy of life.

26
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,440
Because Jake knew how to plan and pull off major heists.

27
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:20,580
But he realized that none of it actually made him happy.

28
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:23,260
That's why, when we first meet Jake in the series,

29
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:25,240
he has already learned the first virtue

30
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:26,540
of his philosophy of life.

31
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:28,060
Can you guess what it is?

32
00:01:28,260 --> 00:01:30,620
Listen to this. Jake starts the series

33
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:33,260
as a companion on the show's adventures,

34
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:34,760
happy just watching the clouds

35
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:35,780
or playing the violin.

36
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:37,840
From that very first moment,

37
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:39,980
everything about Jake seems simple.

38
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,340
The way he talks, the way he solves problems,

39
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,280
even the way he deals with danger.

40
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:46,360
While everyone else makes plans and strategies,

41
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:48,100
Jake simply trusts his instincts,

42
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:50,940
using his powers to do what he thinks is best.

43
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:52,240
If it works, great.

44
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:54,060
And if it doesn't, that's fine too.

45
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:55,700
Just try something else.

46
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:58,360
He doesn't overthink what it means to be good,

47
00:01:58,360 --> 00:01:59,520
brave, or worthy.

48
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:01,660
He just keeps things simple and clear.

49
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:04,420
Help your friends, be honest, and enjoy the present moment.

50
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:07,480
In an age where everyone makes everything complicated,

51
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:09,340
Jake shows us another way.

52
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:11,660
Take the witch's garden, for example.

53
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:13,660
That's where Jake loses his powers.

54
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,220
But listen to what he says.

55
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:19,320
Adventuring is pretty hard for a guy like me without superpowers.

56
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:20,860
I'm not an adventurer anymore.

57
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:23,100
From now on, I'm just an old dog.

58
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:25,160
Jake doesn't get angry about what happened.

59
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:26,360
He doesn't despair either.

60
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:28,860
Instead, he treats losing his powers like the weather.

61
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,420
Something happens, and you simply have to adapt.

62
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:34,100
But this goes deeper than we might think.

63
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:36,360
Jake isn't simply giving up and doing nothing.

64
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:38,840
He's focusing on what he can do

65
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,580
and what he can control.

66
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:45,660
And that leads to his first virtue: simplicity. It's present everywhere in his life.

67
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,380
But first, let's look at Finn.

68
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:52,760
Finn is often busy proving his worth, but Jake teaches him that maybe that's not the right path.

69
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:56,800
Hey, being bad at something is the first step toward getting good at it.

70
00:02:57,160 --> 00:03:02,180
That means your worth doesn't disappear just because you can't do something or solve a problem.

71
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:04,720
It's completely normal to be bad at something at first.

72
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,900
That's the first step toward getting good.

73
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:11,680
And being good or bad at something doesn't make you more or less valuable as a person.

74
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,700
But once you realize that and learn to be humble, that's when you start improving,

75
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,780
even if you doubted yourself before.

76
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:22,400
In the episode "Puhoy," while Finn worries about alternate universes and different versions of himself,

77
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:25,140
Jake grabs his favorite cup and throws it out the window.

78
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:27,320
This is my favorite cup.

79
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:33,360
Now it's gone forever, so it's not real anymore, and I don't care about it.

80
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:35,920
That's pure Stoicism from Jake,

81
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:40,180
built around the idea that we suffer more when we focus on things we can't control.

82
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:44,100
But the greatest example of his simplicity comes in the episode "Jake the Dog."

83
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:48,220
There, he meets Prismo, a cosmic being who can grant any wish.

84
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:51,480
Now tell me, if you were him, what would you wish for?

85
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:54,060
Infinite power to solve every problem in the world?

86
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:56,720
Immortality? Or maybe becoming the smartest person alive?

87
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:59,580
Jake? Jake just wishes for a sandwich.

88
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:02,000
I really wish I had a sandwich.

89
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,260
Prismo is confused.

90
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:06,180
But Jake is absolutely thrilled to get his sandwich.

91
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:07,920
He doesn't need anything more.

92
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:09,420
And that shows us that

93
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:11,580
happiness doesn't increase just because you have more.

94
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:13,680
It depends on how you see things

95
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,860
and the value you place on the present moment.

96
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:18,060
Because when you could have everything,

97
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:21,320
choosing what you actually want is what makes you truly happy.

98
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:23,360
So don't make life more complicated than it needs to be.

99
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,600
Keep it simple.

100
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:27,360
Focus on what's real and what you can control.

101
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,400
Your friends.

102
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,800
Your happiness in the present.

103
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,540
And what you can do right now.

104
00:04:31,540 --> 00:04:33,540
Everything else is just noise.

105
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:36,540
But simplicity is only the beginning of Jake's philosophy of life.

106
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:39,640
His second virtue is what truly brings life to even the most ordinary moments.

107
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:42,020
Even in the most mundane moments,

108
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:44,240
or rather, especially in those moments.

109
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:46,240
So what exactly is that virtue?

110
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:49,020
Well, let's look at the episode "Time Sandwich."

111
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:52,080
There, Jake gets philosophical before making lunch.

112
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:56,180
Now I'm ready to receive the guidance of the great creative kingdom

113
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:57,700
for the sandwich I'm about to create.

114
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:00,500
May your kingdom come, along with all the loaves of bread.

115
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:04,260
He treats the ordinary act of cooking with the kind of importance

116
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:06,060
that most people reserve for special occasions.

117
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:08,140
And that's his second virtue:

118
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:08,920
joy.

119
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:11,720
More specifically, joy in the little things.

120
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,720
It's not toxic positivity

121
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,620
or forcing yourself to enjoy everything.

122
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:17,980
It's about treating even the most ordinary moments

123
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:19,260
as something special,

124
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:21,100
and giving them your full attention.

125
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:23,600
And Jake takes that idea to another level.

126
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,100
Take the episode "Jake the Brick."

127
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:27,820
It's probably the most important episode for understanding Jake's way of life.

128
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:34,280
There, he decides to spend a few days as a brick, just to know what it feels like when a brick wall collapses.

129
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:38,460
Most people would see that as a waste of time or something incredibly boring.

130
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:40,920
But to Jake, it's almost like a dream.

131
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:46,540
When I was a kid, I always wanted to know what it would feel like to be a brick in a brick shack when the walls came crashing down.

132
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:53,140
When Jake tells the story of what happened in the forest, he turns a simple observation into something almost like a spiritual poem.

133
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:57,280
A little rabbit building its nest becomes a reflection on purpose and impermanence.

134
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:01,220
And the collapsing wall becomes a symbol of learning to let go.

135
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:03,560
Letting go into the peaceful forest.

136
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:07,240
A little bird doesn't understand the struggles it causes, and somehow soothes them.

137
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:12,040
But the best thing about Jake's joy is the way he spreads it to the people around him.

138
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:15,940
In "Dad's Dungeon," Finn and Jake have fun with all the shapes Jake transforms into.

139
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:19,960
Okay, let me try turning into a pepper-spray leopard.

140
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:25,720
Finn can't stop laughing.

141
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:29,580
Because Jake's joy spreads naturally, without any effort.

142
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:30,880
It just spreads everywhere.

143
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:33,740
Just like when he suddenly starts singing,

144
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:36,120
Hot cakes are good, hot cakes are great.

145
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:38,640
I make them better than bacon.

146
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:41,860
He's simply turning whatever he's doing into an improvised little song,

147
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:43,900
something we've all done at some point.

148
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:46,340
And honestly, it's a pretty great song.

149
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:49,520
Hot cakes are good, just a tasty treat for me.

150
00:06:50,650 --> 00:06:53,670
Like Jake, we need to learn how to feel joy

151
00:06:53,670 --> 00:06:55,070
even in the smallest things.

152
00:06:55,270 --> 00:06:56,630
Because if you can do that,

153
00:06:56,870 --> 00:06:59,050
you'll find that your days become a little better.

154
00:06:59,350 --> 00:07:02,370
But those two virtues are only the beginning of Jake's philosophy of life,

155
00:07:02,810 --> 00:07:03,890
which goes much deeper.

156
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:07,550
You see, Jake knows how to understand other people's pain,

157
00:07:07,770 --> 00:07:10,070
something almost no one else in Adventure Time can do.

158
00:07:10,370 --> 00:07:12,350
And that's what his third virtue is all about.

159
00:07:12,670 --> 00:07:16,050
And "Princess Cookie" is the perfect episode to understand it.

160
00:07:16,350 --> 00:07:17,190
To understand it better,

161
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:19,550
there's a cookie named Baby Snaps

162
00:07:19,550 --> 00:07:21,550
who takes hostages after getting angry with Bonnie

163
00:07:21,550 --> 00:07:24,030
for mocking her dream of becoming a princess.

164
00:07:25,890 --> 00:07:28,530
Jake listens to her story and immediately understands.

165
00:07:28,790 --> 00:07:31,490
While everyone else sees a criminal who needs to be stopped,

166
00:07:31,490 --> 00:07:34,470
Jake sees a little cookie whose dream has been shattered,

167
00:07:34,470 --> 00:07:36,810
and then he does something completely unexpected.

168
00:07:37,310 --> 00:07:39,750
Instead of completing the mission and arresting the cookie,

169
00:07:40,090 --> 00:07:44,290
Jake helps her escape, choosing compassion and personal humanity over blindly following the rules,

170
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:46,090
which, in this case, would have been meaningless.

171
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:49,550
That moment reveals something fundamental about Jake's empathy,

172
00:07:49,550 --> 00:07:51,070
his third virtue.

173
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:54,970
His empathy is especially directed toward people who are looked down on by society.

174
00:07:54,970 --> 00:07:57,090
Because when he sees them suffering,

175
00:07:57,090 --> 00:07:59,670
Jake's loyalty shifts from completing the mission

176
00:07:59,670 --> 00:08:01,990
to helping the people who genuinely need him.

177
00:08:01,990 --> 00:08:05,370
But that empathy has also gotten him into trouble.

178
00:08:05,370 --> 00:08:09,050
When Jake had children, he tried to become the loving,

179
00:08:09,050 --> 00:08:10,710
responsible father he thought he should be.

180
00:08:10,710 --> 00:08:12,390
So he became overprotective.

181
00:08:12,390 --> 00:08:15,870
The problem was that his children didn't need nearly that much protection.

182
00:08:16,150 --> 00:08:18,530
They grew up and matured incredibly fast.

183
00:08:18,630 --> 00:08:21,750
Within just a few days, they could do things better than their own father.

184
00:08:22,030 --> 00:08:23,830
So eventually, Jake let them go.

185
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:28,410
This upset Kim Kil Whan because he wanted his father to take things more seriously.

186
00:08:28,670 --> 00:08:30,390
We're in serious trouble, Dad.

187
00:08:30,570 --> 00:08:32,110
It's time you faced it.

188
00:08:32,410 --> 00:08:34,130
Get a job. Stop messing around.

189
00:08:34,390 --> 00:08:36,150
But instead of becoming defensive,

190
00:08:36,430 --> 00:08:39,490
Jake realized that his strength wasn't being a strict father,

191
00:08:39,490 --> 00:08:43,410
but being present in his children's lives and supporting them however he could.

192
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:45,630
And by doing that, he won Kim Kil Whan over,

193
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:48,570
giving his son genuine love through his presence,

194
00:08:48,870 --> 00:08:51,970
rather than simply being a responsible father. And that's wisdom.

195
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:56,790
Jake always pays attention to what's actually happening instead of thinking about what he believes should happen,

196
00:08:57,170 --> 00:08:58,890
and that's how he developed genuine empathy.

197
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:02,430
More importantly, he gives that same freedom to other people.

198
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:04,690
He doesn't expect anyone to be perfect or easy to understand.

199
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:07,330
He simply accepts people for who they are,

200
00:09:07,330 --> 00:09:09,370
without forcing them to become who he wants them to be.

201
00:09:09,370 --> 00:09:12,050
That way, he lets everyone live their own lives,

202
00:09:12,050 --> 00:09:14,190
while living his own life as well.

203
00:09:14,190 --> 00:09:15,930
And that taught him something

204
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,770
that most people never learn.

205
00:09:17,770 --> 00:09:19,670
That lesson is his fourth virtue

206
00:09:19,670 --> 00:09:21,110
in his philosophy of life,

207
00:09:21,110 --> 00:09:23,170
and perhaps the most important one.

208
00:09:23,170 --> 00:09:25,590
And now you'll see exactly what it is.

209
00:09:25,590 --> 00:09:28,130
Let's take a look at "Ocarina."

210
00:09:28,130 --> 00:09:30,050
He shows up late to his children's birthday party,

211
00:09:30,050 --> 00:09:32,750
and even brings them a bag of beef pasta.

212
00:09:32,750 --> 00:09:34,250
Happy birthday, kids.

213
00:09:34,250 --> 00:09:35,910
Dad brought you some food.

214
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:40,350
In anyone else's eyes, Jake is failing as a father,

215
00:09:40,350 --> 00:09:42,470
and there's really no excuse for it.

216
00:09:42,470 --> 00:09:44,650
And yet, all of his children,

217
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:48,890
except for one, are still happy to see him for a reason I mentioned earlier.

218
00:09:48,890 --> 00:09:53,150
When Jake is there, he is truly present, giving them his full attention and energy.

219
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:55,350
And that's his fourth virtue:

220
00:09:55,350 --> 00:09:56,390
presence.

221
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:58,350
During the card game between father and daughter,

222
00:09:58,350 --> 00:10:01,350
Jake says one of the wisest things he's ever said,

223
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:03,570
a line that perfectly captures this virtue.

224
00:10:03,570 --> 00:10:14,390
Jake realizes that every stage of life calls for a different way of living,

225
00:10:14,390 --> 00:10:18,630
and worrying about where you've been or where you're going will only make you miserable.

226
00:10:18,930 --> 00:10:21,190
So Jake chooses to be present instead of overthinking.

227
00:10:21,610 --> 00:10:26,270
He enjoys the present moment and becomes the person others need, someone who is truly there.

228
00:10:26,550 --> 00:10:29,230
That's why everyone loves being around Jake,

229
00:10:29,590 --> 00:10:32,310
but there's still one more virtue needed to complete his philosophy of life.

230
00:10:32,310 --> 00:10:34,370
A virtue that may be the most important one for many people.

231
00:10:34,370 --> 00:10:36,290
See if you can figure out what it is.

232
00:10:36,290 --> 00:10:39,630
In "The New Land," Jake has a prophetic dream about his own death.

233
00:10:39,630 --> 00:10:48,980
Most people would panic over something like that.

234
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:51,040
They'd despair over the fact that the end was coming.

235
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:54,220
In fact, Finn does exactly that when Jake tells him about the dream.

236
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:55,940
But what Jake does is rather surprising.

237
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:57,060
Nothing.

238
00:10:57,060 --> 00:11:00,420
He's calm, and he's even curious about what will happen.

239
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:02,880
Dude, you just gotta accept it.

240
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:05,700
While Finn desperately tries to stop the dream from coming true,

241
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:08,320
Jake doesn't try to run away or find a solution.

242
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:10,940
He simply accepts what seems to be his fate.

243
00:11:10,940 --> 00:11:22,860
In that way, he sees his own death the same way he saw losing his powers or his favorite cup,

244
00:11:22,860 --> 00:11:27,040
as something that happens outside his control and something he has to accept.

245
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:30,120
Acceptance. That's his final virtue.

246
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:33,960
And in the episode "Together Again," Jake takes that idea to its absolute limit.

247
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:42,540
There, Prismo is erased from existence, and the only way to bring him back is for Jake to sacrifice himself forever, but he doesn't even hesitate.

248
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:48,020
It shows that sometimes doing what's right requires personal sacrifice, and Jake understands that.

249
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:55,660
But his acceptance appears in many other moments too, like when Kito captures him and locks him away, or when he asks Finn to accept his death.

250
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:58,520
It's okay. This is where I'm supposed to be.

251
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:03,140
And that acceptance eventually leads him to spiritual enlightenment in the afterlife.

252
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:04,480
Jake is completely at peace,

253
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,140
beyond human understanding

254
00:12:06,140 --> 00:12:07,360
and personal desires,

255
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:09,700
existing in a state of cosmic consciousness.

256
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,680
This is the ultimate achievement:

257
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:12,940
becoming one with the universe.

258
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,420
But Jake's final decision

259
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:16,180
makes everything even more interesting.

260
00:12:16,180 --> 00:12:18,540
Because when Jake sees Finn suffering from loss

261
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:19,900
and struggling to let go,

262
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:21,700
he decides to leave the afterlife

263
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:23,600
so he can be reincarnated alongside his friend.

264
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,840
Because that's what matters to him:

265
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:27,560
living alongside his brother.

266
00:12:27,560 --> 00:12:29,600
Jake, what are you doing?

267
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:31,620
I just achieved my ultimate enlightenment.

268
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:32,680
I know.

269
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:35,300
I came back just for fun.

270
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:37,960
Because being alive with you is awesome.

271
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,220
Jake giving up spiritual perfection

272
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:42,520
just to be with Finn is genuinely beautiful.

273
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:44,620
Because it perfectly captures who this dog really is,

274
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:46,900
and who he has always been:

275
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:49,360
someone who knows how to enjoy the simple things in life

276
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:50,880
and accept them as they are.

277
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:52,300
But you know what?

278
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:55,080
There's an even more beautiful way Jake shows his acceptance.

279
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:57,800
It's in his relationship with Aquarius.

280
00:12:57,800 --> 00:13:00,460
Jake learned Korean because Aquarius only speaks Korean.

281
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:03,820
And he never asked her to change or learn his language.

282
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:06,040
Instead, he accepted their differences

283
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:09,060
and adapted so he could fully be there for her.

284
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:11,260
Living in her world in their own way.

285
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:13,280
That's acceptance in love.

286
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:15,780
And that's the essence of Jake the Dog:

287
00:13:15,780 --> 00:13:17,760
someone who accepts his own limitations

288
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:19,360
but never wastes his life.

289
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,740
Someone who accepts that

290
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:22,420
he can't control everything,

291
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:23,980
but still does what he wants to do.

292
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:25,420
Someone who accepts that

293
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:26,980
heaven can be a lonely place,

294
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:30,460
and therefore chooses an imperfect connection with his brother.

295
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:33,280
And someone who accepts the person he loves for who she truly is,

296
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:36,220
willing to adapt to their differences so he can love her fully.

297
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:39,400
That's Jake's philosophy of life: live first, think later.

298
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:43,160
But then why would a god choose to live like a mortal?

299
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:47,620
Because throughout the series, Jake learns that life isn't about achieving

300
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:49,920
great things or possessing all the power in the world,

301
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:53,320
but about being present in every moment and finding joy in the little things,

302
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:56,420
accepting whatever happens without ever stopping yourself from loving.

303
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:58,420
And that's what I want you to do too.

304
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,660
Live every day as if it were your last,

305
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:02,540
and savor every sandwich,

306
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:05,280
every moment as if it were a gift from the universe,

307
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:07,740
as if it were something that would become an eternal memory.

308
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:09,020
Because I can assure you,

309
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:09,860
it will.